{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Adjusting to a New Place", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "  Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety  of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/>         The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to do away with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to remove something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to fall back on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to use in times of difficulty\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to live up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to fulfill expectations\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look forward to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to eagerly anticipate something\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Does it live up to your standards?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We basically do away with lunch altogether during the week here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Fortunately, we can fall back on our own meals at the restaurant!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Position of Not", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In English, the adverb  <span class=\"italic\">not</span> usually goes after the auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d to form the negative. <br/><br/> You can use the adverb not in other positions in some cases.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, we find the adverb not in conjunction with an auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d in a negative sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">It's  <span class=\"strong\">not</span> cheap, but it's very practical.<br/> Lunch is  <span class=\"strong\">not</span> something I like to miss!<br/> I don't really see my roommates = I do  <span class=\"strong\">not</span> really see my roommates.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the long form instead of the contraction, you emphasize the negation of the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You also find <span class=\"italic\">not</span> <span class=\"strong\">before</span> a verb in the Infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">People always find an excuse  <span class=\"strong\">not</span> to have lunch at work.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to do away with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remove something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We do away with having a lunch break during the week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear about adjusting to a new environment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to fall back on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use in times of need", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fortunately, we can fall back on our own meals at the restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to live up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fulfill expectations", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Does your accommodation live up to your expectations?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to look forward to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to eagerly anticipate something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm looking forward to the weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "personal space", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the space surrounding a person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have enough personal space in my house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "communal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "common use, shared by all members of a community", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our house has one communal bathroom among three roommates.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "isolated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "far away from other things, places or people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a foreigner, I feel isolated living in Japan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write about the differences in culture between your country and a country you know well. You may have to do research on one. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find a least five differences and give your opinion on them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain your opinion using the position of not.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the differences to your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about manners and customs. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give my opinion on the manners and customs. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my opinion. ", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about manners and customs. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about life experiences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain my opinion. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " If you had to live abroad, what would you miss most from home? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How long do you usually have lunch for every day?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"con